{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaQaJS4r8xZR3vacxXo5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I replaced the `sorry` in `Main.lean` with a proof, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\n```lean\ntheorem myLen_map (f : α → β) (xs : List α) : myLen (xs.map f) = myLen xs := by\n  induction xs with\n  | nil => rfl\n  | cons x xs ih => simp [List.map, myLen, ih]\n```\n\nThe proof uses induction on `xs`:\n- **Empty list:** both sides reduce to `0` by definition, so `rfl` closes it.\n- **Non-empty list (`x :: xs`):** unfolding `List.map` and `myLen` gives `myLen (xs.map f) + 1 = myLen xs + 1`. The induction hypothesis `ih` says the two lengths are equal, and `simp` uses it to finish the goal."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":436,"cache_read_input_tokens":7861,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":436},"output_tokens":282,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0524d8fc-78f6-4c29-967e-dbf1e0a53d45","uuid":"5ca2daa6-9bf0-442c-a3d2-a0e7195f66af","timestamp":"2026-10-31T13:38:40.822Z","request_id":"req_011CgaQaJ3jiXCxC5iy5bx1R"}
